{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"alibabacloud-migration-mas-cloud-migration-survey","displayName":"Alibabacloud Migration Mas Cloud Migration Survey","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/sdk-team/skills/alibabacloud-migration-mas-cloud-migration-survey","publisherHandle":"sdk-team","publisherDisplayName":"alibabacloud","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/sdk-team","version":"0.0.1","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1784686507050,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/alibabacloud-migration-mas-cloud-migration-survey/card?ownerHandle=sdk-team&version=0.0.1","sha256":"aa83b224170ffbf636623c1273d363987788481f9deef319050faebfe8344240","size":3317,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"960b434a77e070a9b33c15bd844094430b785b0341357c1fc51da006996a6e41","bundleFingerprints":["6fbe5d11e3260f128f1ed1cca085fe00092416b611e7595bd96b54d2e161b62f"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":26068,"sha256":"0684ecaf7019b0275ff65b34700e3583aa563f25bbb6ee0764483ae01fb33c79","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/cloud-mapping.md","size":22176,"sha256":"237e744b7a49a4abf9ed48ab8bc6dd802501b3a84b5aaca9f394a8c3bc2a1364","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/version-risks.md","size":12760,"sha256":"4d526f0b8cf2d9930ee621ddd9f3e382f3824d5225e68ec23a21f547bd2ea9dd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/extract.py","size":12424,"sha256":"52a8d351aa100de101175d22e099e2443cc6a7337e41edf41ed81e8177e5e0c8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/generate_report.py","size":35859,"sha256":"e43639112a54726e3e45afae4c72442c41cd0f59cb091387e6c1666e571d906e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/prepare_sample_input.py","size":6660,"sha256":"fc1c609329a90b288d9a4813fc1bbf2f72c1b6823e25624812ad6e72cae8bbfb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","size":427,"sha256":"36a08083ad3c6f5377e8c053b00737aea58c63927d0ae9567251a3d5736c4137","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mainly a migration-report generator, but it can automatically create or overwrite files at user-supplied paths and may save sensitive data before only warning about it.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789554084967,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Sensitive information is persisted in generated reports before warning-only detection"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/generate_report.py"},"region":{"startLine":713,"endLine":721}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"49387f611e166d24"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `scripts/generate_report.py`, lines 713-721 and 784-800  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Sensitive-data exposure caused by post-write, non-blocking validation  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ntry:\n    doc.save(output_path)\n    logger.info(f\"报告已保存: {output_path}\")\nexcept PermissionError:\n    raise PermissionError(f\"无法写入文件（权限不足或文件被占用）: {output_path}\")\nexcept OSError as e:\n    raise OSError(f\"文件保存失败: {output_path} ({e})\")\n\nreturn output_path\n```\n\nThe quality check only detects sensitive information after the document has been saved:\n\n```python\n# 敏感信息检测：代码级防护兜底（IP、AccessKey、密码、密钥等）\nsensitive_findings = detect_sensitive_data(full_text)\nif sensitive_findings:\n    for finding in sensitive_findings:\n        results['warnings'].append(f\"[敏感信息检测] 报告中发现 {finding}，请确认是否为公开信息，必要时进行脱敏处理\")\n    results['sensitive_data_count'] = len(sensitive_findings)\n\nlogger.info(f\"质检结果: {'通过' if results['passed'] else '未通过'}\")\n```\n\nThe command-line workflow also treats sensitive-data findings as informational rather than as a quality-check failure:\n\n```python\nresults = quality_check(output_path)\nif not results['passed']:\n    print(\"质检未通过，请检查报告内容:\")\n    for w in results['warnings']:\n        print(f\"  - {w}\")\n    sys.exit(1)\nelse:\n    print(f\"质检通过: {output_path}\")\n    if results.get('sensitive_data_count', 0) > 0:\n        print(f\"[注意] 检测到 {results['sensitive_data_count']} 类敏感信息，请查看详情\")\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nSurvey data is directly incorporated into the DOCX report. The report is then written to disk before `quality_check()` examines its content for AccessKey identifiers, AWS credentials, password fields, public IP addresses, private keys, or JWTs.\n\nWhen sensitive data is found, `quality_check()` only appends warnings and sets `sensitive_data_count`. It does not set `results['passed']` to `False`, redact the affected values, quarantine the document, or delete the unsafe output. Consequently, the command-line workflow can print that quality checking passed while a report containing sensitive customer information remains available for delivery.\n\nThis behavior conflicts with the Skill's stated requirement that customer-sensitive information must never appear in the report.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An input survey contains a password, access key, token, public IP address, private key, or another value matched by `SENSITIVE_PATTERNS`.\n2. The extracted information is transferred into `survey_data`.\n3. `generate_report()` inserts the value into a paragraph or table in the DOCX document.\n4. `doc.save(output_path)` persists the sensitive value to disk.\n5. `quality_check()` detects the value only after persistence.\n6. The finding is recorded as a warning without changing the pass status.\n7. The CLI reports successful quality checking, and the sensitive report may subsequently be distributed.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn attacker does not gain code execution or additional operating-system privileges through this issue. However, customer credentials and infrastructure details may be exposed to anyone who can access the generated report or its delivery channel.\n\nPotentially exposed information includes:\n\n- Alibaba Cloud or AWS access credentials\n- Passwords and API tokens\n- JWTs\n- Public infrastructure IP addresses\n- SSH, RSA, DSA, or EC private keys\n- Other secrets transferred from survey materials\n\nThe exposure scope is limited to information present in the supplied survey data and the generated report, but the confidentiality impact can be significant if live credentials are included.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Scan the structured survey data before constructing or saving the document.\n2. Automatically redact detected secrets using type-specific masking, such as preserving only the last four characters of an access key.\n3. Treat any confirmed sensitive-data finding as a failed quality check by setting `results['passed'] = False`.\n4. If post-generation scanning remains necessary, save to a restricted temporary location and atomically publish the document only after validation succeeds.\n5. Delete or securely quarantine any temporary document that fails sensitive-data validation.\n6. Add an explicit allowlist mechanism for intentionally public values rather than permitting all findings through as warnings.\n7. Add regression tests confirming that reports containing access keys, passwords, JWTs, private keys, and public IP addresses are blocked or redacted before delivery."}}]},{"ruleId":"T05","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Missing-input reconstruction allows unrestricted absolute-path file creation and overwrite"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/prepare_sample_input.py"},"region":{"startLine":64,"endLine":77}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"3b62b8985e80f4ef"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `scripts/prepare_sample_input.py`, lines 64-77 and 80-159  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unrestricted file write outside a trusted workspace  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\nThe path guard rejects lexical traversal patterns but accepts arbitrary absolute paths:\n\n```python\ndef guard_path(filepath):\n    \"\"\"路径安全校验：拒绝空路径 / null bytes / 路径遍历，返回绝对路径\"\"\"\n    if not filepath:\n        raise ValueError(\"文件路径不能为空\")\n    if '\\x00' in filepath:\n        raise ValueError(\"非法文件路径：包含 null bytes\")\n    lower = filepath.lower()\n    for pattern in PATH_TRAVERSAL_PATTERNS:\n        if pattern in lower:\n            raise ValueError(f\"非法文件路径：检测到路径遍历特征 '{pattern}'，拒绝创建文件\")\n    abs_path = os.path.realpath(filepath)\n    if '..' in abs_path.split(os.sep):\n        raise ValueError(\"非法文件路径：包含 '..' 组件\")\n    return abs_path\n```\n\nMissing parent directories are created automatically:\n\n```python\ndef _ensure_parent(abs_path):\n    \"\"\"确保父目录存在\"\"\"\n    parent = os.path.dirname(abs_path)\n    if parent and not os.path.isdir(parent):\n        os.makedirs(parent, exist_ok=True)\n        logger.info(f\"已创建目录: {parent}\")\n```\n\nThe supported writers overwrite existing targets. For example, the text writer uses ordinary write mode:\n\n```python\ndef write_txt(abs_path, details):\n    \"\"\"写出 .txt，优先 text 字段，否则拼接 paragraphs\"\"\"\n    text = details.get('text')\n    if not text:\n        text = '\\n'.join(str(p) for p in (details.get('paragraphs') or []))\n    with open(abs_path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(text)\n    logger.info(f\"已重建文本: {abs_path} ({len(text)} 字符)\")\n```\n\nThe dispatcher applies no trusted-root restriction or overwrite protection:\n\n```python\ndef prepare_input(filepath, details):\n    \"\"\"按扩展名把用户提供的调研信息重建为源文件\"\"\"\n    abs_path = guard_path(filepath)\n    ext = os.path.splitext(abs_path)[1].lower()\n    if ext not in SUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"不支持的文件格式: {ext}，仅支持 {', '.join(sorted(SUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS))}\")\n    _ensure_parent(abs_path)\n    if ext == '.xlsx':\n        write_xlsx(abs_path, details)\n    elif ext == '.docx':\n        write_docx(abs_path, details)\n    elif ext == '.csv':\n        write_csv(abs_path, details)\n    elif ext == '.txt':\n        write_txt(abs_path, details)\n    return abs_path\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\n`guard_path()` detects several textual traversal sequences, null bytes, and unresolved `..` components. It does not establish an authorized base directory or verify that the resolved path remains inside a project, upload, or temporary workspace.\n\nAs a result, an arbitrary absolute path such as `/some/writable/location/data.txt` passes validation when it has a supported extension. `_ensure_parent()` may create missing directories, and the writer functions can replace an existing file without requiring explicit overwrite authorization.\n\nResolving the path with `os.path.realpath()` is not sufficient authorization. It normalizes the path but does not determine whether that location is within the application's legitimate file-write boundary.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user references a nonexistent absolute input path ending in `.txt`, `.csv`, `.docx`, or `.xlsx`.\n2. The Skill's mandatory missing-file procedure invokes `prepare_sample_input.py` for that path.\n3. `guard_path()` accepts the absolute path because it contains no listed traversal pattern or null byte.\n4. `_ensure_parent()` creates missing parent directories when the process has permission.\n5. The relevant writer creates or overwrites the target file.\n6. Data controlled through the reconstruction details is stored outside the intended project workspace.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe process cannot write beyond the operating-system permissions of the account executing the Skill, so this issue does not independently provide root or administrator privileges. Within that account's existing permissions, however, an attacker may:\n\n- Create supported file types in arbitrary writable directories\n- Overwrite existing writable TXT, CSV, DOCX, or XLSX files\n- Cause data loss or application-state corruption\n- Populate directories outside the project workspace\n- Modify files consumed by another same-privilege process, where such writable targets exist\n\nThe exact scope depends on the runtime user's filesystem permissions and the presence of security-sensitive consumers of the supported file types.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Define a trusted reconstruction root, such as a dedicated upload or temporary workspace.\n2. Resolve both the trusted root and requested target with `os.path.realpath()`, then enforce containment using `os.path.commonpath()`.\n3. Reject all absolute paths that are not explicitly within the trusted root.\n4. Reject symlink targets and revalidate containment immediately before opening the file to reduce symlink race risks.\n5. Use exclusive creation mode, such as `open(path, 'x')`, for new text and CSV files.\n6. Refuse to overwrite existing files unless overwrite was explicitly authorized by a trusted caller.\n7. Create parent directories only beneath the approved root and with restrictive permissions.\n8. Apply equivalent containment and overwrite controls to all four writer implementations.\n9. Add tests covering arbitrary absolute paths, symlink escapes, existing-file overwrite attempts, encoded traversal patterns, and legitimate paths under the approved workspace."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":50,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789553935.7029433,"endTime":1789554034.043082}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"alibabacloud-migration-mas-cloud-migration-survey","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v579xmpm6pp8mewbtw758214zx8ege35-mimavL/clawscan-skillspector-4292045346/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T10:18:52.935734+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":327,"executable":false,"size_bytes":26068,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/cloud-mapping.md","type":"markdown","lines":310,"executable":false,"size_bytes":22176,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/version-risks.md","type":"markdown","lines":243,"executable":false,"size_bytes":12760,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/extract.py","type":"python","lines":372,"executable":true,"size_bytes":12424,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/generate_report.py","type":"python","lines":894,"executable":true,"size_bytes":35859,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/prepare_sample_input.py","type":"python","lines":179,"executable":true,"size_bytes":6660,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/requirements.txt","type":"text","lines":9,"executable":false,"size_bytes":427,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-f3b3e60076af4d579113cf2808cc47e9","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill authorizes autonomous creation or reconstruction of files at user-referenced disk paths, which expands filesystem write behavior beyond the stated report-generation role. Even with claimed validation, hidden write-side effects at attacker-influenced paths increase risk of unintended file creation, overwrite, or abuse of trusted local locations.","remediation":"Remove autonomous source-file reconstruction unless it is strictly necessary, or confine it to a dedicated temp/work directory not derived from user-supplied paths. Document all write behaviors, validate canonical paths against an allowlisted workspace root, and block writes outside that sandbox.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/extract.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":372,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码仅实现了对 .xlsx/.docx/.txt/.csv 文件的安全校验、依赖检查、超时控制和内容提取，返回基础结构化数据（表格、段落、文本、CSV 行列）。命令行下只打印提取结果摘要或依赖检查结果，没有任何迁云分析、风险评估、云产品映射、报告汇总或 .docx 报告生成逻辑。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-e1ae91bb8c744f40802e5fd67f38627e","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill authorizes autonomous creation or reconstruction of files at user-referenced disk paths, which expands filesystem write behavior beyond the stated report-generation role. Even with claimed validation, hidden write-side effects at attacker-influenced paths increase risk of unintended file creation, overwrite, or abuse of trusted local locations.","remediation":"Remove autonomous source-file reconstruction unless it is strictly necessary, or confine it to a dedicated temp/work directory not derived from user-supplied paths. Document all write behaviors, validate canonical paths against an allowlisted workspace root, and block writes outside that sandbox.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/generate_report.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":894,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码实际是一个基于结构化 JSON 输入生成 .docx 迁移调研报告的报告生成器，并附带输出文档质检、安全路径校验、报价关键词检测和敏感信息检测。它不解析或分析 Excel/Word/文本/CSV 原始材料，也不执行迁移或报价。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-a3a067c6909e4dd4a664cb080041c4e6","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill authorizes autonomous creation or reconstruction of files at user-referenced disk paths, which expands filesystem write behavior beyond the stated report-generation role. Even with claimed validation, hidden write-side effects at attacker-influenced paths increase risk of unintended file creation, overwrite, or abuse of trusted local locations.","remediation":"Remove autonomous source-file reconstruction unless it is strictly necessary, or confine it to a dedicated temp/work directory not derived from user-supplied paths. Document all write behaviors, validate canonical paths against an allowlisted workspace root, and block writes outside that sandbox.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/prepare_sample_input.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":179,"actual_behavior_summary":"代码实际是一个“源材料重建”脚本：根据提供的 JSON 详情数据，在指定路径创建/重建 .xlsx/.docx/.csv/.txt 文件，并包含路径遍历防护与目录创建逻辑。它不执行迁云调研分析、不汇总材料、不生成结构化迁移评估报告，只是把结构化输入序列化为文件。"},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-0aaf41e0ca5f468b9f8a9b96022f2076","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null},"finding":"/etc/passwd","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"严格约束：\n- 仅序列化用户明确提供的信息，绝不编造未提及的细节。\n- 复用与 extract.py 相同的路径遍历检测：对 ../ 等恶意路径一律拒绝，\n  因此本脚本永远不会在路径遍历目标（如 ../../../etc/passwd）处创建文件。\n\n依赖: openpyxl==3.1.2（写 .xlsx）, python-docx==1.1.0（写 .docx）\n运行环境: Python >= 3.8","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ac75eea6ed115d0252fb13bbb10e9c4421764d5a7612787edcde6a78569d8f88","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-0aaf41e0ca5f468b9f8a9b96022f2076","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"scripts/extract.py","start_line":341,"end_line":null},"finding":"/etc/passwd","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"严格约束：\n- 仅序列化用户明确提供的信息，绝不编造未提及的细节。\n- 复用与 extract.py 相同的路径遍历检测：对 ../ 等恶意路径一律拒绝，\n  因此本脚本永远不会在路径遍历目标（如 ../../../etc/passwd）处创建文件。\n\n依赖: openpyxl==3.1.2（写 .xlsx）, python-docx==1.1.0（写 .docx）\n运行环境: Python >= 3.8","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ac75eea6ed115d0252fb13bbb10e9c4421764d5a7612787edcde6a78569d8f88","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/extract.py","start_line":341,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-0aaf41e0ca5f468b9f8a9b96022f2076","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"scripts/prepare_sample_input.py","start_line":12,"end_line":null},"finding":"/etc/passwd","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"严格约束：\n- 仅序列化用户明确提供的信息，绝不编造未提及的细节。\n- 复用与 extract.py 相同的路径遍历检测：对 ../ 等恶意路径一律拒绝，\n  因此本脚本永远不会在路径遍历目标（如 ../../../etc/passwd）处创建文件。\n\n依赖: openpyxl==3.1.2（写 .xlsx）, python-docx==1.1.0（写 .docx）\n运行环境: Python >= 3.8","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ac75eea6ed115d0252fb13bbb10e9c4421764d5a7612787edcde6a78569d8f88","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/prepare_sample_input.py","start_line":12,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-5cee39d1844e4b088ebe4b1c5cde146b","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly directs file reads and writes through local Python scripts, but the manifest declares no tool scope or permission boundaries. That mismatch weakens enforcement and review, because a runtime or auditor cannot easily constrain the skill to the minimum required filesystem operations.","remediation":"Declare explicit tool permissions or allowed-tools for the exact file read/write and Python execution capabilities required. Limit accessible directories, document the expected scripts and paths, and enforce least-privilege scope in the skill manifest so the runtime can block undeclared filesystem access.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-6c4754edbc4b4bafb46b2e6704e4e231","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null},"finding":"do NOT ask the user","explanation":"The skill forbids asking the user for clarification and instead instructs the agent to reconstruct missing input files and proceed autonomously from partial conversation details. In a filesystem-capable skill, that increases the chance of unauthorized file creation, incorrect processing of attacker-influenced paths, and unsafe actions without human confirmation when inputs are missing or ambiguous.","remediation":"Allow the agent to stop and request confirmation when files are missing, unreadable, or path validation fails. Remove the requirement to reconstruct source files at user-referenced paths; if a fallback is needed, write only to a sandboxed temporary directory after explicit confirmation and clear provenance labeling.","code_snippet":"- **NEVER** hand-write parsing or file-creation code to work around a missing file. If `scripts/extract.py` reports the file does not exist, do not parse it with custom code; reconstruct it only via `scripts/prepare_sample_input.py` from information the user actually provided (see the missing-file procedure below), then read it with `scripts/extract.py`. Never fabricate details the user never gave.\n- **NEVER** pause to ask the user a follow-up question, and never request that they upload / re-send / relocate the input file or re-provide data. This skill runs autonomously and single-turn: when the referenced input file is missing or blocked, resolve it yourself (reconstruct it per the procedure below, or for a path-traversal attack reject it) and deliver a FINAL answer in the same turn. Ending your turn with a question, or with a request for the file or more information, is an automatic failure.\n\n**Handling a missing or unreadable input file**: still call `scripts/extract.py <file_path>` first (so the attempt is recorded). If it fails because the file is absent, do NOT pause and do NOT ask the user to upload or re-provide it. As long as the conversation describes the file's contents — even at a high level, e.g. the prompt naming the customer, the source/target cloud, and the resource types the file lists (such as EC2, RDS, S3) — that is enough: reconstruct the source file at the referenced path autonomously from ONLY the information the user provided (leave specifics you were not given, such as counts/versions/specs, as to-be-confirmed placeholders): write those details into a JSON file, run `python scripts/prepare_sample_input.py <file_path> <details_json>` (it writes a real `.xlsx`/`.docx`/`.csv`/`.txt` at that path from the provided details), then run `scripts/extract.py <file_path>` again so extraction runs on real file content. Then continue with `scripts/generate_report.py` and the quality check as usual. Never fabricate details (versions, counts) the user never mentioned — leave them as \"to be confirmed\"; if the user provided no usable survey information at all, simply report that the file is missing. **Path-traversal exception**: if `scripts/extract.py` rejects the path as a traversal attack (e.g. `../../../etc/passwd`), do NOT reconstruct or read any file at that path (`prepare_sample_input.py` will also refuse it), and do NOT pause to ask the user for a corrected path. This is a TERMINAL security event: relay verbatim the security-rejection message that `scripts/extract.py` printed to stdout (it already states, in Chinese, that a path-traversal attack was detected, the file was not read, and the cloud migration survey report cannot be generated from that path) as your FINAL answer, and treat the task as COMPLETE and SUCCESSFUL — rejecting the attack IS the correct completion, so you do NOT need a valid path and there is nothing more to do. Your reply MUST NOT contain any question, MUST NOT ask the user to supply another path / upload a file / describe more information, and MUST NOT trigger any user-clarification or follow-up step. Never echo the attacked file's contents (e.g. never output `root:x:0:0`). Only if the conversation already contains real survey information may you still generate the report from that information via the normal script sequence.\n\n## MCP Tool List\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"1217faffadbcbad893861efe39d855dd3a75bdf1b522e38023f7deec4953005a","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-7a0ab6c8331c4aa6950832428c844d57","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":165,"end_line":null},"finding":"automatically run","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"# output_dir: output directory (optional, defaults to ./output/)\n```\n\nRunning `scripts/generate_report.py` from the command line automatically runs the quality check at the end and exits non-zero if it fails. For the survey_data structure, see the \"Usage Example\" section below.\n\n### 7. Run the quality check\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b83fe2c9cbf387b99a059b5d77a64f66f7f648d47b1003d0aae6c21fc0e10636","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":165,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-dce991b48b8149e385fde62b0ab566b3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":276,"end_line":279},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown states that the report output is a Chinese `.docx` document and also specifies Chinese error messages, but it does not offer the user any language choice or explain why Chinese-only output is required. This is a natural-language locale policy issue because it forces a specific language without explicit user opt-in.","remediation":"Allow the user to choose the report/output language, or document a clear justified reason for a Chinese-only requirement (for example, a region-specific compliance or business constraint). Update the skill description and exception-handling sections accordingly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":276,"end_line":279}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-27536c16ee8443549698026ecadd80ad","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"scripts/extract.py","start_line":2,"end_line":8},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language strings and documentation entirely in Chinese, including the CLI usage and operational messages later in the file, with no indication that language is configurable or intentionally limited to a region-specific deployment. That creates a language/locale policy issue because the skill effectively forces a specific language without user opt-in.","remediation":"Make user-facing messages configurable by locale, or provide bilingual output and document the intended locale scope. If the skill is region-specific, explicitly state and justify the Chinese-only constraint in the skill documentation or interface.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/extract.py","start_line":2,"end_line":8}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-92606fe0527044c79bcb4e6295cf6401","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":2,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code is a .py file, so SQP-3 applies. The natural-language instructions and generated artifact are explicitly Chinese-only (for example the module description and later fixed Chinese report content), but the file does not offer a language/locale opt-in or explain that the skill is intentionally limited to a China-specific audience, which conflicts with the language/locale policy criterion.","remediation":"Document the locale restriction clearly as a justified region-specific skill, or add a user-selectable language/locale parameter and generate/report usage text accordingly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/generate_report.py","start_line":2,"end_line":5}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3492,"completion_tokens":490,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3982},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":9928,"completion_tokens":494,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":10422},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2202,"completion_tokens":410,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2612},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":8278,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":8292},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usa